 "transcript": "Why can the same website load faster in one city than another? One reason is distance. A content delivery network keeps copies of selected files, like images and scripts closer to users. Your request can reach a nearby copy instead of the distant original server. But not everything can be cached forever. When content changes, those copies need rules for updating. Faster delivery also means keeping copies correct.",
